     "parent": "geometry",
     "desc": "Point-line incidence bound (1983): m points + n lines in the plane share at most O((mn) 2/3 + m + n) incidences. Build the Erdős tight construction — a thin K × 2K 2 grid plus K 3 lines — and watch the ratio I/(mn) 2/3 sit flat at 2 −2/3 . The seed crystal that the polynomial-method trilogy grew out of.",
