   "desc": "A box to rant into, and the words end up in your own repo as standard.site records—so any reader on the network can index them. Written entirely in Rust: a workers-rs edge worker and a wasm-bindgen browser module over one shared engine, which is why the preview and the published page cannot disagree. Eleven predicate views give every post alternate readings with real URLs—skeleton strips the function words, spine keeps one sentence per paragraph, cadence draws the shape instead of the text, reverse starts at the conclusion—descended from read's reading modes and composable ( ?view=skeleton+bionic ). Link cards are rasterised at the edge and drawn from the post's own cadence. Subscribe writes a record to your repo; there is no subscriber list here. Agents get MCP, llms.txt and JSON—read and draft, never publish.",
